Algorithm: Contact Management System
Main

Step 1: START. Create an empty doubly linked list, an array of 10 free slots and an empty stack.

Step 2: Display the menu: Add, Delete, Search, Display forward, Display backward, Slot status, Undo delete, Delete history, Exit.

Step 3: Read the choice and call the matching function.

Step 4: Repeat Steps 2 and 3 until choice = 9. STOP.

Add Contact

Step 5: Find the first free slot in the array. If none is free, display “No slots available” and stop.

Step 6: Read contact ID. If the ID already exists in the list, stop.

Step 7: Read name and phone number.

Step 8: Create a new node and insert it at the end of the list (update tail and prev/next links).

Step 9: Mark the slot as occupied and increase count.

Delete Contact

Step 10: Read contact ID and search the list from head. If not found, display “Contact not found” and stop.

Step 11: Push the contact record onto the stack (top = top + 1).

Step 12: Free the contact’s slot in the array.

Step 13: Delete the node by linking its previous and next nodes (update head or tail if needed).

Step 14: Decrease count.

Search Contact

Step 15: Read the contact ID.

Step 16: Traverse the list from head using next until NULL.

Step 17: If a node matches, display the contact details; otherwise display “Contact not found”.

Display Contacts

Step 18: Forward: start at head and print each node using next until NULL.

Step 19: Backward: start at tail and print each node using prev until NULL.

Undo Last Delete

Step 20: If the stack is empty, or no slot is free, display a message and stop.

Step 21: Pop the top record (top = top - 1).

Step 22: Insert the contact at the end of the list and mark a free slot as occupied.

Slot Status and Delete History

Step 23: Slot status: traverse the slot array and print each slot as Free or Occupied.

Step 24: History: print the stack records from top to 0 (latest delete first).

This follows the same step pattern as your Hospital algorithm and matches your latest code (doubly linked list, array and stack). Beds became slots, discharge became delete, and exit is choice = 9.
